
P18-V01 MessageDecoder signature crosswalk — 2026-10-22 20:15 UTC

Compared all 26 public method signatures in the pinned Java fixture
`messageDecoderPublicApi` against the Common crate's exported message functions.
The API map now groups each Java overload with its Rust encoder, decoder,
property, ID, CRC, or compact-message counterpart and links the invoked
fixture coverage. This is a docs-only inventory update; no tests were run.

One boundary remains explicit for future audit: Rust's
`create_message_id_from_host_bytes(&[u8], ...)` returns the same ID for supported
IPv4/IPv6 host bytes, but its immutable-slice API does not model Java's mutable
scratch `ByteBuffer` position side effects. Determine whether that behavior is
part of the compatibility contract before closing the related API row.
